DESIGN DECISIONS
----------------
1. job_03 FIRST_VALUE fix
   FIRST_VALUE window function cannot be combined with tumbling GROUP BY in Flink SQL.
   Replaced with MAX(province) — deterministic, same GROUP BY scope, Flink-compatible.

2. job_04 CEP approach
   MATCH_RECOGNIZE requires Flink CEP JAR not included in our image.
   Used equivalent: tumbling 10-min window COUNT >= 3 for Pattern A,
   simple WHERE taxable_income > 500000 for Pattern B. Both emit to fraud-signals topic.

3. flink-sql-client entrypoint
   Changed from ["bin/sql-client.sh"] (one-shot, exits) to ["tail", "-f", "/dev/null"]
   (keep-alive) so submit_flink_jobs.py can repeatedly exec into the container.
   Removed profile: ["tools"] so the container starts as part of the default stack.

4. kpi-poller service
   Uses python:3.11-slim (no custom build) with pip install at startup.
   Polls PostgreSQL tax_kpi_windows every 30 s, writes Redis HASHes with 15 min TTL.
   Also writes tax:kpi:latest summary key for single-read dashboard access.

5. submit_flink_jobs.py
   - Reads all job_*.sql files in /flink-jobs/
   - Renders ${VAR} placeholders from environment / .env
   - Writes rendered SQL to /tmp/<job>.sql inside flink-sql-client container
   - Executes /opt/flink/bin/sql-client.sh -f <path>
   - Emits OpenLineage START / COMPLETE / FAIL events per job
   - Per-job lineage metadata maps each job to correct input/output datasets

